DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("e^((5-x))");
$fun_1 = Formula("sqrt((((x)^(1/2))+10))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_3 = Compute("(-infinity, 10) U ([1, 14])");
$set_ans_4 = Compute("((-infinity, 10)) - ((-infinity, infinity) - ({-1, 1} U (-infinity, 10))) - ((-infinity, infinity) - ({-1, 1} - ((-infinity, infinity) - [1, 14])))");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("({4, 5, 6, 10}) U {4, 5, 6, 10}");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("[2, 7] U ({4, 5, 6, 10} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {4, 5, 6, 10}))");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

[`15/3+14`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>Real(19.),width=>9}
---

What is the value of [`16+9*6`]? [_____]{Real(70.)}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | 2 \leq x \leq 7\}`]
- [`B = \{4, 5, 6, 10\}`]

Compute:
- [`(B) \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`A \cup (B \cap B) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x < 10\}`]
- [`B = \{-1, 1\}`]
- [`C = \{x | 1 \leq x \leq 14\}`]

Compute:
- [`A \cup (C) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}
- [`(A) \cap (B \cup A) \cap (B \cap C) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 3, -4, -3 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -5, 7, -6 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<3, -4, -3>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<3, -4, -3>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-5, 7, -6>") x Compute("<3, -4, -3>")}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<3, -4, -3>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<3, -4, -3>") . Compute("<-5, 7, -6>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 4, -4, -6 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 7, 6, 2 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -6, -10, -7 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<7, 6, 2>") . Compute("<-6, -10, -7>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-6, -10, -7>"))}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<4, -4, -6>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-6, -10, -7>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<4, -4, -6>") x Compute("<7, 6, 2>")}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f'(2) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>2)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
